 "note": "Ruling Q8. Op target: CheckPreviewTarget checks the repository of a cleanup preview (contract S15, POST /api/cleanup-policies/preview) against the format of the policy (key format): the repository exists, is no group, and has the format of the policy unless the policy format is *; else 400 at repository with the code preview-repository, and the message names the reason: does not exist, is a group, or the two formats. An empty name is a repository that does not exist; its message asks for a name. Names are compared as they are. Op policy: PreviewPolicy turns the refusals of the criteria check (CheckCriteria with no stored criteria, as for a create) and of the policy format check (CheckPolicyFormat with the key formatCheck, when the case has one) into the form of a preview: each field gets the prefix policy., so the ids are policy.criteria.<name>, policy.criteria and policy.format, as the contract names the ids of a preview. The test joins the two results with errors.Join. Ruling Q15: the format of a cleanup policy is one of *, maven2, npm, docker and raw, compared as it is. Op format: CheckFormatValue refuses a create or save with another value, the empty one included, with 400 at format and the code format-unknown; the message names the value and the five formats. The key stored holds the format of the stored policy on a save, and a format the stored policy holds is never refused (ruling R6). Op preview: the whole check of a preview, the criteria and the format value of the policy through PreviewPolicy, joined with CheckPreviewTarget. An unknown format is refused at policy.format, and that check comes before the check of the preview target, so such a preview gets no refusal at repository, also for a repository that does not exist or is a group. The repositories below are the snapshot of every case; demo-maven names the cleanup policy demo-policy.",
